  "verdict": "NO EXPOSURE OSCILLATION AT THIS CADENCE. The mean-luma autocorrelation decays smoothly (lag 1 +0.642 -> lag 6 -0.626) with no negative trough at lag 2-3, which is the signature of a slow settling ramp (10.79 counts of span) rather than a hunting loop, and the character delta ACCUMULATES with lag instead of collapsing -- the opposite of the previous run's flat ~55% profile with a single dip at lag 5.",
  "consequence": "The camera's gain still moves WITH the character delta across lags (correlation +0.992), so a capture whose exposure is not locked still mixes camera and subject in the delta. But the gain here is a slow settling ramp, not a hunt, and the character delta grows with lag the way real change does. The previous run's verdict -- 'EXPOSURE OSCILLATION, the delta is dominated by the camera's AGC' -- was measured on a torn signal and does not survive; this capture is NOT unusable for motion work on the grounds of an exposure hunt. Locking exposure is still worth doing, as a control rather than as a rescue.",
